window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Pursued by a relentless assassin, Alan and Jinny race across the galaxy in search of a secret truth that has eluded humanity for centuries.</p> <p>The 47 colonies have been at peace for over 700 years. But nothing is as it seems. The Council government of all humanity controls the populace through lies, fear, and genetically-engineered agents who do its terrible bidding: fearsome Enacter hitmen incapable of questioning orders and trained to kill without mercy; mind Readers who can see your memories with a brush of the hand; Blenders who take on the appearance of even those you love; and Speakers who can convince even a jaded populace that their lies ring true.</p> <p>In this dystopian far future, the one seemingly bright spot is the Guard, a policing force that maintains peace and order throughout human space. Detective Alan Daily was proud to be part of their ranks and to find his life’s meaning in protecting humanity from the darkness. But now, that darkness has come for him!</p> <p>When Alan and his partner investigate a rash of mysterious suicides, it thrusts them into a web of deceit that ends with his partner dead and Alan on the run from the very organization he has dedicated his life to. His only hope lies with the beautiful and enigmatic Jinny Ambrosa. A powerful and dangerous Reader with a terrible secret of her own, she will lead him deep into a world of rebels, space pirates, hidden navies, and desperate freedom fighters.</p> <p>On their tail is Tyrus Tyne, the Council’s most effective assassin and Enacter. Fueled by his own dark past, he will stop at nothing to keep our heroes from exposing the Council’s lies. With allies dying all around them, can Jinny and Alan reach the end of their journey before darkness falls for all mankind, or will they fail to find the truth of the Four Worlds in time?</p> <p><i>The Truth</i> is the epic first volume of an imaginative and immersive science fiction series, equally suitable for adults and YA, that will take you on a fast-paced thrill ride.</p>"; 
